{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#781","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#781","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#781\",\"parent_revision\":\"429d2b72ff1f37d73b5acd7532fc223adf87c7a29b2ef79c67e5ff126083d0ce\",\"root_revision\":\"429d2b72ff1f37d73b5acd7532fc223adf87c7a29b2ef79c67e5ff126083d0ce\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n**Current state**: Task readiness in the SAM system is determined solely by dependency graph resolution: a task is \\\"ready\\\" when its status is NOT STARTED and all dependency tasks have status COMPLETE. There is no mechanism to express conditional readiness based on observable system state (e.g., \\\"file X exists\\\", \\\"command Y exits 0\\\", \\\"field Z in config has value V\\\"). Acceptance criteria in task files are free-text prose that agents interpret; they are not machine-evaluable conditions.\\n\\nFile: `plugins/python3-development/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` -- the `get_ready_tasks` function checks only `status` and `dependencies` fields. No condition evaluation exists.\\n\\n**Target state**: Task YAML frontmatter supports an optional `conditions` field containing a list of 3-token expressions in the format `scope.field op value` (e.g., `file.plan/architect-auth.md exists true`, `command.uv_run_tests exit_code 0`). The `sam ready` command evaluates these conditions alongside dependency checks. A task is \\\"ready\\\" only when both dependency graph and all conditions pass. The condition evaluator is a standalone function that can be tested independently.\\n\\n**Measurable signal**: Run: `uv run sam ready P{N}` on a plan where a task has `conditions: [\\\"file.some/path.md exists true\\\"]` -- output includes or excludes the task based on whether the file exists. The `conditions` field is documented in `.claude/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: SAM Declarative condition syntax for task readiness\\nDate: 2026-04-23\\nGoal: Extend task readiness logic to evaluate a declarative `conditions` list alongside dependency graph resolution.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. get_ready_tasks function location | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py \u2014 checks status + dependencies only\\n2. Task model fields | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py \u2014 Task class; no conditions field currently\\n3. TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md documentation | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md \u2014 needs conditions field documented\\n4. 3-token expression format design | AVAILABLE (documented) | scope.field op value: file.PATH exists true, command.CMD exit_code N \u2014 from description\\n5. Condition evaluator implementation | DERIVABLE | standalone function; file-exists and command-exit-code are the two mandatory scope types\\n6. Edge cases: missing file, command timeout, non-zero exit on first attempt | DERIVABLE | needs specification before coding\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 format well-specified; implementation straightforward for file and command scopes.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `Task` model includes optional `conditions: list[str] | None` field in `sam_schema/core/models.py`\\n- [ ] `get_ready_tasks` evaluates `conditions` alongside dependency graph: a task with unsatisfied conditions is NOT included in ready list even if dependencies are met\\n- [ ] Supported condition formats: `file.PATH exists true`, `file.PATH exists false`, `command.CMD exit_code N` (N is int)\\n- [ ] `uv run sam ready P{N}` on a plan where T2 has `conditions: [\\\"file.plan/architect.md exists true\\\"]` excludes T2 when the file is absent, includes it when present\\n- [ ] Condition evaluator is a standalone function with independent unit tests\\n- [ ] `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` documents the `conditions` field and 3-token format with examples\\n- [ ] `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` \u2014 zero errors\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Task model (add conditions field)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` \u2014 get_ready_tasks (add condition evaluation)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 document conditions field\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/` \u2014 unit tests for condition evaluator and get_ready_tasks integration\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a **SAM plan designer**, I want **tasks to support a `conditions` field with 3-token expressions** so that **a task is not dispatched until system state (file exists, command exits 0) is observable \u2014 preventing race conditions caused by dependency graph alone**.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **sam: declarative condition syntax for task readiness** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/tori-cli.md -- pattern: 3-token condition format for task conditions\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"90f7206f79eab66c431a755778a4ea1e07f0eecf2fc378274471a5b9a7b5f5f8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTET6g\"}"}